#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:458 400.en.adoc:822
#, no-wrap
msgid "type"
msgstr "tipo"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:461
msgid "https://dwc.tdwg.org/list/#dc_type[dc:type]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:463
msgid "The nature of the resource. Use `StillImage` if the record is based on an image or sequence of images, `MovingImage` if based on a video. One can also use the broader term `Image` for all records."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:465
#, no-wrap
msgid "license"
msgstr "licencia"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:468
msgid "https://dwc.tdwg.org/list/#dcterms_license[dcterms:license]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:470
msgid "The licence under which the data record is shared. Very likely this will be the same licence as the one used for the dataset as a whole, but it is possible to deviate cite:[waller-2020]. To enable wide use, we recommend publishing data under a https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/[Creative Commons Zero waiver] and to provide it as a URL: `https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode`. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with the `path` of the licence that has the scope `data` in {package-licenses}, although there it is specified for the dataset as whole, rather than per record."
msgstr "La licencia bajo la cual se comparte el registro de datos. Probablemente esta será la misma licencia que la utilizada para el conjunto de datos pero es posible desviar cite:[waller-2020]. Para permitir un uso amplio, recomendamos publicar datos bajo una https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/[exención Creative Commons Zero] y proporcionarlo como una URL: `https://creativecommons.org/publicodomain/cero/1.0/legalcode`. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde a la `ruta` de la licencia que tiene los `datos` del ámbito en el {package-licenses}, aunque allí se especifica para el conjunto de datos en lugar de por registro."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:472
#, no-wrap
msgid "rightsHolder"
msgstr "Titular de derechos"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:475
msgid "https://dwc.tdwg.org/list/#dcterms_rightsHolder[dcterms:rightsHolder]"
msgstr "https://dwc.tdwg.org/list/#dcterms_rightsHolder[dcterms:rightsHolder]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:477
msgid "The person or organization (i.e. <<participant>>) owning or managing rights over the resource. In all likeness the organization that decided under what license the data are published and/or the publisher of the data (i.e. the organization selected as publisher when registering a dataset with GBIF). Use an acronym if the organization has one. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with the `title` of the collaborator that has the role `rightsHolder` in {package-contributors}."
msgstr "La persona u organización (es decir, <<participant>>) que posee o gestiona los derechos sobre el recurso. Con toda probabilidad, la organización que decidió bajo qué licencia se publican los datos y/o el editor de los datos (es decir, la organización seleccionada como editora al registrar un conjunto de datos con GBIF). Utilice un acrónimo si la organización tiene uno. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con el `título` del colaborador que tiene el rol `tendedordeDerechos` en {package-contributors}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:479
#, no-wrap
msgid "datasetID & datasetName"
msgstr "datasetID & datasetName"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:482
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:datasetID] & term:dwc[dwc:datasetName]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:datasetID] & term:dwc[dwc:datasetName]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:484
msgid "Respectively the identifier and name of the dataset. For term:dwc[dwc:datasetID] we recommend using a stable URL or identifier that allows users to find information about the source dataset/study. In order of preference: dataset DOI (`https://doi.org/10.15468/5tb6ze`), study URL (`http://n2t.net/ark:/63614/w12001317`), or study identifier used by the <<data-management-system,data management system>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {package-id}, unless a better identifier is available (e.g. a DOI). term:dwc[dwc:datasetName] should refer to the title of the dataset/study as referred to by term:dwc[dwc:datasetID]. We recommend using the same value for the title in the metadata. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {package-title}."
msgstr "Respectivamente el identificador y el nombre del conjunto de datos. Para term:dwc[dwc:datasetID] recomendamos usar una URL o identificador estable que permita a los usuarios encontrar información sobre el conjunto de datos/estudio de origen. En orden de preferencia: conjunto de datos DOI (`https://doi.org/10. 5468/5tb6ze`), estudio URL (`http://n2t. et/ark:/63614/ w12001317`), o identificador de estudio utilizado por el <<data-management-system,data management system>>. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {package-id}, a menos que haya un identificador mejor disponible (p. ej., un DOI). term:dwc[dwc:datasetName] debe referirse al título del conjunto de datos/estudio como se refiere por term:dwc[dwc:datasetID]. Recomendamos usar el mismo valor para el título en los metadatos. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {package-title}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:486
#, no-wrap
msgid "collectionCode"
msgstr "códigoDeLaColección"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:489
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:collectionCode]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:collectionCode]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:491
msgid "The name or acronym identifying the collection or dataset the record was derived from. Traditionally used to indicate a physical collection, we recommend to provide the name of the <<data-management-system,data management system>> (i.e. virtual collection) the record was derived from. This allows users to search for records from the same data management system across datasets. Recommended values: `Agouti`, `Camelot`, `eMammal`, `Trapper`, `Wildlife Insights`, etc. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with the `title` of the (applicable) source in {package-sources}."
msgstr "El nombre o acrónimo que identifica la recolección o conjunto de datos de los que se derivó el registro. Tradicionalmente se utiliza para indicar una colección física, recomendamos proporcionar el nombre del <<data-management-system,data management system>> (es decir, colección virtual) de la que derivó el registro. Esto permite a los usuarios buscar registros del mismo sistema de gestión de datos a través de conjuntos de datos. Valores recomendados: `Agouti`, `Camelot`, `eMammal`, `Trapper`, `Wildlife Insights`, etc. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde al `título` de la fuente (aplicable) en {package-sources}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:493
#, no-wrap
msgid "basisOfRecord"
msgstr "baseDelRegistro"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:496
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:basisOfRecord]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:basisOfRecord]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:498
msgid "The specific nature of the record. Set to `MachineObservation` for all records. While humans decide when and were to deploy a camera trap, and humans or machines (AI) can <<classification,classify>> media, the capturing of the record is done by a machine responding to a sensor. This is critically different from human observations, where a human is actively in control of the decision whether to record an organism or not."
msgstr "La naturaleza específica del registro. Establecer en `MachineObservation` para todos los registros. Mientras que los humanos deciden cuándo y cuándo desplegar una cámara trampa, y los humanos o las máquinas (IA) pueden <<classification,classify>> archivos, la captura del registro es realizada por una máquina que responde a un sensor. Esto es críticamente diferente de las observaciones humanas, donde un humano controla activamente la decisión de registrar o no un organismo."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:500
#, no-wrap
msgid "dataGeneralizations"
msgstr "generalizacionesDeLosDatos"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:503
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:dataGeneralizations]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:dataGeneralizations]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:505
msgid "The actions taken to make the published data less specific or complete than in its original form. We recommend succinctly describing here what <<section-sensitive-information,sensitive information>> of the record was generalized and how. Note that this information can be provided at record level and does not need to apply to the whole dataset. If important information was omitted altogether, use term:dwc[dwc:informationWithheld]."
msgstr "Las acciones emprendidas para hacer que los datos publicados sean menos específicos o completos que en su forma original. Recomendamos describir concisamente aquí qué <<section-sensitive-information,sensitive information>> del registro fue generalizada y cómo. Tenga en cuenta que esta información se puede proporcionar a nivel de registro y no necesita aplicarse a todo el conjunto de datos. Si la información importante fue omitida por completo, utilice term:dwc[dwc:informationWithheld]."

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:507 400.en.adoc:591 400.en.adoc:627 400.en.adoc:698
#: 400.en.adoc:720
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr "Ejemplos:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: 400.en.adoc:511
#, no-wrap
msgid "coordinates rounded to 0.001 degree\n"
"scientific name generalized to genus\n"
msgstr "coordenadas redondeadas a 0,001 grados\n"
"nombre científico generalizado a género "

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:514 400.en.adoc:808
#, no-wrap
msgid "occurrenceID"
msgstr "identficadorDelRegistro"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:517 400.en.adoc:811
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceID]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceID]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:519
msgid "An identifier for the <<observation>>. Use a <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-observationID}."
msgstr "Un identificador para la <<observation>>. Utilice un i<<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. En Camtrap DP, este término se corresponde con {observations-observationID}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:521
#, no-wrap
msgid "individualCount"
msgstr "conteoIndividual"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:524
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:individualCount]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:individualCount]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:526
msgid "The number of observed <<individual,individuals>>. Note that this number is dependent on the <<table-classification-precision,precision>> of the identifications. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-count}."
msgstr "El número de <<individual,individuals>>. Tenga en cuenta que este número depende de la <<table-classification-precision,precision>>. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {observations-count}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:528
#, no-wrap
msgid "sex"
msgstr "sexo"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:531
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:sex]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:sex]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:533
msgid "The sex of the observed <<individual>>(s). We recommend using the controlled values `male` and `female`, which are based on Camtrap DP and compatible with the https://rs.gbif.org/vocabulary/gbif/sex.xml[GBIF Sex vocabulary]. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-sex}."
msgstr "El sexo de los <<individual>>s observados. Recomendamos usar los valores controlados `macho` y `hembra`, que se basan en el Camtrap DP y son compatibles con el vocabulario de sexo GBIF [https://rs. bif.org/ vocabulary/gbif/sex.xml]. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con https://rs.gbif.org/vocabulary/gbif/sex.xml[GBIF Sex vocabulary]. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-sex}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:535
#, no-wrap
msgid "lifeStage"
msgstr "etapa de vida"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:538
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:lifeStage]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:lifeStage]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:540
msgid "The life stage of the observed <<individual>>(s). We recommend using the controlled values `adult`, `subadult`, and `juvenile`, which are based on Camtrap DP and compatible with the https://registry.gbif.org/vocabulary/LifeStage[GBIF LifeStage vocabulary]. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-lifeStage}."
msgstr "La etapa de vida de los <<individual>>s observados. Recomendamos utilizar los valores controlados `adulto`, `subadulto` y `juvenil`, que se basan en el Camtrap DP y son compatibles con el https://registry.gbif.org/vocabulary/LifeStage[vocabulario GBIF LifeStage]. En Camtrap DP, este término se corresponde con {observations-lifeStage}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:542
#, no-wrap
msgid "behavior"
msgstr "comportamiento"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:545
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:behavior]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:behavior]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:547
msgid "The dominant behaviour of the observed <<individual>>(s). We recommend using existing or your own controlled values (e.g. grazing, browsing, rooting, vigilance, running, walking). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-behavior}."
msgstr "El comportamiento dominante de los <<individual>>s observados. Recomendamos el uso de valores controlados existentes o los suyos propios (por ejemplo, pastando, paciendo, hocicando, vigilando, corriendo, caminando). En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {observations-behavior}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:549
#, no-wrap
msgid "occurrenceStatus"
msgstr "estadoDelRegistro"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:552
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceStatus]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceStatus]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:554
msgid "A statement about the presence or absence of the taxon at a location. When reduced to species observations (filtering out <<blank,blanks>>, etc.), camera trap data only contain presence records. Set to `present` for all records."
msgstr "Una declaración acerca de la presencia o ausencia del taxón en una ubicación. Cuando se reduce a observaciones de especies (filtrando <<blank,blanks>>, etc.), los datos de la cámara trampa solo contienen registros de presencia. Establecer en `presentar` para todos los registros."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:556
#, no-wrap
msgid "occurrenceRemarks"
msgstr "comentariosSobreElRegistro"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:559
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceRemarks]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceRemarks]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:561
msgid "The comments or notes about the <<observation>>. These are typically notes (sometimes in the native language of the author) about the observation and/or observed <<individual>>(s) that were not or could not be recorded in another field. This information is potentially useful to publish, but may contain <<section-other-sensitive-information,sensitive information>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-observationComments}."
msgstr "Los comentarios o notas sobre la <<observation>>. Estas normalmente son notas (a veces en el idioma nativo del autor) sobre la observación y/o el <<individual>> observado que no fue o no pudo ser registrado en otro campo. Esta información es potencialmente útil para publicar, pero puede contener <<section-other-sensitive-information,sensitive information>>. En Camtrap DP, este término se corresponde con {observations-observationComments}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:563
#, no-wrap
msgid "organismID"
msgstr "ID de organismo"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:566
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:organismID]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:organismID]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:568
msgid "An identifier for an observed and known <<individual>> that was recognized by colour ring, ear tag, skin pattern or other characteristics. Observations with term:dwc[dwc:organismID] typically have term:dwc[dwc:individualCount] of 1, unless the term:dwc[dwc:organismID] refers to a known group. Unless a globally unique identifier is available and known for the individual, we recommend using the code/identifier assigned within the camera trap study to the individual, allowing users to find all observations of this individual within the dataset. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-individualID}."
msgstr "Un identificador para un <<individual>> observado y conocido que fue reconocido por el anillo de colores, la etiqueta del oído, el patrón de la piel u otras características. Las observaciones con term:dwc[dwc:organismID] normalmente tienen term:dwc[dwc:individualCount] de 1, a menos que el term:dwc[dwc:organismID] se refiera a un grupo conocido. A menos que un identificador único esté disponible y sea conocido por el individuo recomendamos usar el código/identificador asignado dentro del estudio de cámaras trampa al individuo, permitiendo a los usuarios encontrar todas las observaciones de este individuo dentro del conjunto de datos. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {observations-individualID}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:570
#, no-wrap
msgid "eventID"
msgstr "identificadorDelEvento"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:573
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:eventID]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:eventID]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:575
msgid "An identifier for the event the observation belongs to. We recommend providing the identifier for the <<event>> (typically a <<sequence>>) as used for <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,event-based classification>>. Using an Occurrence core, events will not have their own records, but providing their identifier in term:dwc[dwc:eventID] allows users to find all observations (and media) for a specific event. Use a <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. Note that GBIF.org will automatically group observations with the same term:dwc[dwc:eventID] as belonging together. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-eventID}."
msgstr "Un identificador para el evento al que pertenece la observación. Recomendamos proporcionar el identificador para el <<event>> (normalmente una <<sequence>>) como se usa para una <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,event-based classification>>. Usando un Núcleo de ocurrencia, los eventos no tendrán sus propios registros, pero proporcionar su identificador en term:dwc[dwc:eventID] permite a los usuarios encontrar todas las observaciones (y medios) para un evento específico. Utilice un <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. Tenga en cuenta que GBIF.org agrupará automáticamente observaciones con el mismo term:dwc[dwc:eventID] que pertenecen juntos. En Camtrap, este \ttérmino\t se corresponde \tcon \t{observations-eventID}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:577
#, no-wrap
msgid "parentEventID"
msgstr "IDdeEventoOriginal"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:580
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:parentEventID]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:parentEventID]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:582
msgid "An identifier for a broader event then those identified by <<section-eventid,eventID>>. We recommend providing the identifier of the <<deployment>>. Using an Occurrence core, deployments will not have their own records, but providing their identifier in term:dwc[dwc:parentEventID] allows users to find all observations (and media) for a specific deployment. Use a <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. Note that GBIF.org will automatically group observations with the same term:dwc[dwc:parentEventID] as belonging together. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-deploymentID}."
msgstr "Un identificador para un evento más amplio que los identificados por <<section-eventid,eventID>>. Recomendamos proporcionar el identificador del <<deployment>>. Usando un Núcleo de ocurrencia, los despliegues no tendrán sus propios registros, pero proporcionar su identificador en term:dwc[dwc:parentEventID] permite a los usuarios encontrar todas las observaciones (y archivos multimedia) para un despliegue específico. Utilice un <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. Tenga en cuenta que GBIF.org agrupará automáticamente observaciones con el mismo term:dwc[dwc:parentEventID] que pertenecen juntos. En Camtrap DP, este término se corresponde \tcon\t {observations-deploymentID}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:584
#, no-wrap
msgid "eventDate"
msgstr "fechaDelEvento"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:587
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:eventDate]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:eventDate]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:589
msgid "The date, date-time or date-time interval during which the <<event>> occurred. We recommend using a single timestamp for <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,media-based classifications>> and an interval - consisting of the timestamps of the start and end of the <<event>> as identified by <<section-eventid,eventID>> for <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,event-based classifications>>. Write timestamps in the ISO 8601 format (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`), use `/` to indicate an interval and include the timezone (`+02:00`) or convert and indicate as UTC (`Z`). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-eventStart} and {observations-eventEnd}, or {observations-eventStart} if both are equal."
msgstr "La fecha, la fecha-hora o el intervalo fecha-hora durante el que ocurrió el <<event>>. Recomendamos utilizar una única marca de tiempo para <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,media-based classifications>> y un intervalo que consista en las marcas de tiempo del inicio y del final del <<event>> como se identifica por la <<section-eventid,eventID>> para <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,event-based classifications>>. Escriba las marcas de tiempo en formato ISO 8601 (`AAAA-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`), utilice `/` para indicar un intervalo e incluir la zona horaria (`+02:00`) o convertir e indicar como UTC (`Z`). En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde a {observations-eventStart} y {observations-eventEnd}, u {observations-eventStart} si ambos son iguales."

#. type: delimited block -
#: 400.en.adoc:596
#, no-wrap
msgid "2020-07-29T05:38:55Z/2020-07-29T05:39:00Z\n"
"2020-07-29T05:38:55Z\n"
"2020-07-29T07:38:55+02:00\n"
msgstr "2020-07-29T05:38:55Z/2020-07-29T05:39:00Z\n"
"2020-07-29T05:38:55Z\n"
"2020-07-29T07:38:55+02:00\n"

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:599
#, no-wrap
msgid "habitat"
msgstr "hábitat"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:602
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:habitat]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:habitat]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:604
msgid "A category or description of the habitat in which the <<event>> occurred. This is typically the habitat at the time of deployment, with values repeated for all records of this deployment. Values can be controlled, ideally using an existing classification system, or free-text descriptions. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-habitat}."
msgstr "Una categoría o descripción del hábitat en el que ocurrió el <<event>>. Este es normalmente el hábitat en el momento de la despliegue, con valores repetidos para todos los registros de este despliegue. Los valores pueden ser controlados, idealmente utilizando un sistema de clasificación existente o descripciones de texto libre. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {deployments-habitat}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:606
#, no-wrap
msgid "samplingProtocol"
msgstr "protocoloDeMuestreo"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:609
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:samplingProtocol]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:samplingProtocol]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:611
msgid "The method(s) or protocol(s) used during the <<event>>. We recommend using the controlled value `camera trap`. This allows users to search for records with this protocol across datasets."
msgstr "Los métodos o protocolos utilizados durante el <<event>>. Recomendamos utilizar el valor controlado `cámara trampa`. Esto permite a los usuarios buscar registros con este protocolo a través de conjuntos de datos."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:613
#, no-wrap
msgid "samplingEffort"
msgstr "esfuerzoDeMuestreo"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:616
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:samplingEffort]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:samplingEffort]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:618
msgid "The amount of effort expanded during the <<event>>. We recommend providing the date-time interval the camera trap was deployed, using the same formatting conventions as <<section-eventdate,eventDate>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-deploymentStart} and {deployments-deploymentEnd}."
msgstr "La cantidad de esfuerzo aumentó durante el <<event>>. Recomendamos proporcionar el intervalo de fecha y hora que se desplegó la cámara trampa, utilizando las mismas convenciones de formato que <<section-eventdate,eventDate>>. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde a {deployments-deploymentStart} y {deployments-deploymentEnd}]."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:620
#, no-wrap
msgid "eventRemarks"
msgstr "comentariosSobreElEvento"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:623
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:eventRemarks]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:eventRemarks]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:625
msgid "The comments or notes about the <<event>>. These are typically notes (sometimes in the native language of the author) about the <<deployment>> that were not or could not be recorded in another field. This information is potentially useful to publish, but may contain <<section-other-sensitive-information,sensitive information>>. We also recommend this term for providing other (structured) information associated with the deployment, such as <<bait>> use, <<feature-type,feature type>> or tags, as pipe (`|`) separated values. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-deploymentComments} and relates to {deployments-baitUse}, {deployments-featureType} and {deployments-deploymentTags}."
msgstr "Los comentarios o notas sobre el <<event>>. Estas normalmente son notas (a veces en el idioma nativo del autor) sobre el <<deployment>> que no fue o no pudo ser registrado en otro campo. Esta información es potencialmente útil para publicar, pero puede contener <<section-other-sensitive-information,sensitive information>>. También recomendamos este término para proporcionar otra información (estructurada) asociada al despliegue, tales como uso de <<bait>>, <<feature-type,feature type>> o etiquetas, como valores separados por barras verticales (`|`). En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {deployments-deploymentComments} y se relaciona con {deployments-baitUse}, {deployments-featureType} y {deployments-deploymentTags}."

#. type: delimited block -
#: 400.en.adoc:632
#, no-wrap
msgid "camera trap with bait near burrow\n"
"camera trap without bait | tags: position:above stream\n"
"camera malfunction on 29/06/2020\n"
msgstr "cámara trampa con cebo cerca de madriguera\n"
"cámara trampa sin cebo | etiquetas: posición:sobre arroyo\n"
"mal funcionamiento de cámara el 29/06/2020"

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:635
#, no-wrap
msgid "locationID"
msgstr "identificadorDeLaUbicación"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:638
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:locationID]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:locationID]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:640
msgid "An identifier for the <<location>>. This identifier allows users to find all observations (and media) for a specific location (across deployments). Use a <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-locationID}."
msgstr "Un identificador para la <<location>>. Este identificador permite a los usuarios encontrar todas las observaciones (y archivos multimedia) para una ubicación específica (a través de despliegues). Utilice un <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde con {deployments-locationID}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:642
#, no-wrap
msgid "locality"
msgstr "localidad"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:645
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:locality]"
msgstr "término:dwc[dwc:locality] (Localidad)"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:647
msgid "The name of the <<location>>. This is typically a name or code assigned within the camera trap study. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-locationName}."
msgstr "El nombre de la <<location>>. Este es típicamente un nombre o código asignado dentro del estudio de la cámara trampa. En Camtrap DP, este término corresponde a {deployments-locationName}."

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:649
#, no-wrap
msgid "minimumDepthInMeters & maximumDepthInMeters"
msgstr "minimumDepthInMeters & maximumDepthInMeters"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:652
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:minimumDepthInMeters] & term:dwc[dwc:maximumDepthInMeters]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:minimumDepthInMeters] & term:dwc[dwc:maximumDepthInMeters]"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:654
msgid "The depth (in meters) below the local surface. For (marine) camera trap studies, this is the <<camera-depth,depth>> at which the <<camera>> is deployed. We recommend providing either a <<camera-depth,camera depth>> or <<camera-height,camera height>>, not both. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-cameraDepth}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:656
#, no-wrap
msgid "minimumDistanceAboveSurfaceInMeters & maximumDistanceAboveSurfaceInMeters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:659
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:minimumDistanceAboveSurfaceInMeters] & term:dwc[dwc:maximumDistanceAboveSurfaceInMeters]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:661
msgid "The height (in meters) above a reference surface. For camera trap studies, this is the <<camera-height,height>> at which the <<camera>> is deployed. We recommend providing either a <<camera-depth,camera depth>> or <<camera-height,camera height>>, not both. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-cameraHeight}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:663
#, no-wrap
msgid "decimalLatitude & decimalLongitude"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:666
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:decimalLatitude] & term:dwc[dwc:decimalLongitude]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:668
msgid "The geographic latitude and longitude of the <<location>>, in decimal degrees. Latitude values lie between -90 and 90, longitude values between -180 and 180. For camera trap studies, these are typically obtained by GPS and recorded in the <<data-management-system,data management system>>. We recommend providing the coordinates as stored in the data management system, unless they need to be rounded/generalization to protect <<section-sensitive-location-information,sensitive information>>. In Camtrap DP, these terms correspond with {deployments-latitude} and {deployments-longitude} respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:670
#, no-wrap
msgid "geodeticDatum"
msgstr "dátumGeodésico"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:673
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:geodeticDatum]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:geodeticDatum] (Dato geodésico)"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:675
msgid "The spatial reference system used for the geographic <<section-decimallatitude-decimallongitude,coordinates>>. For coordinates obtained by GPS this is typically `EPSG:4326` (i.e. `WGS84`) cite:[chapman-wieczorek-2020]. In Camtrap DP, WGS84 is implied for the terms {deployments-latitude} and {deployments-longitude}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:677
#, no-wrap
msgid "coordinateUncertaintyInMeters"
msgstr "incertidumbreDeLaCoordenadaEnMetros"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:680
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:coordinateUncertaintyInMeters]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:coordinateUncertaintyInMeters] (Incertidumbre de las coordenadas en metros)"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:682
msgid "The horizontal distance (in metres) from the geographic <<section-decimallatitude-decimallongitude,coordinates>> describing the smallest circle containing the <<location>>. We recommend `30` meters as reasonable lower limit for coordinates obtained by GPS, but see <<section-location>> for details on what elements contribute to the uncertainty. <<section-sensitive-location-information,Generalized/rounded>> coordinates in particular will increase the term:dwc[dwc:coordinateUncertaintyInMeters]. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-coordinateUncertainty}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:684
#, no-wrap
msgid "coordinatePrecision"
msgstr "precisiónDeLaCoordenada"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:687
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:coordinatePrecision]"
msgstr "term:dwc[dwc:coordinatePrecision] (Precisión de las coordenadas)"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:689
msgid "The decimal precision of the geographic <<section-decimallatitude-decimallongitude,coordinates>>>, if known. This information is known and we recommend providing it for <<section-sensitive-location-information,generalized/rounded>> coordinates (e.g. `0.001` for coordinates that were rounded to 3 decimals). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {package-coordinatePrecision}, although there it is specified for the dataset as whole, rather than per record."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:691
#, no-wrap
msgid "identifiedBy"
msgstr "identificadoPor"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:694
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:identifiedBy]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:696
msgid "The person or <<AI,species classification model>> that identified the observed <<individual,individual(s)>> and assigned the <<section-scientificname,scientificName>>. We recommend providing a single name: that of the person or model that made the (most recent) classification. Although <<classification,classifying>> can be broader than assigning a scientific name, it is likely to involve that aspect for <<observation-type,animal observations>>. Note that this term contains <<section-personal-data,personal data>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-classifiedBy}."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: 400.en.adoc:703
#, no-wrap
msgid "Peter Desmet\n"
"Western Europe species model Version 1\n"
"anonymized:3eb30aa\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:706
#, no-wrap
msgid "dateIdentified"
msgstr "fechaIdentificada"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:709
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:dateIdentified]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:711
msgid "The date or date-time on which the identification was made. We recommend providing a single timestamp: that of the <<classification>> made by the person or model indicated in <<section-identifiedby,identifiedBy>>. This information is typically recorded by the <<data-management-system,data management system>>. Write timestamps in the ISO 8601 format (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`) and include the timezone (`+02:00`) or convert and indicate as UTC (`Z`). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-classificationTimestamp}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:713
#, no-wrap
msgid "identificationRemarks"
msgstr "comentariosSobreLaIdentificación"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:716
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:identificationRemarks]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:718
msgid "The comments or notes about the identification. We recommend using this term to provide information on whether the <<classification>> was made by a human or <<AI,species classification model>> as well as the degree of certainty if available (often recorded for AI classification). In Camtrap DP, this term relates to {observations-classificationMethod} and {observations-classificationProbability}."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: 400.en.adoc:724
#, no-wrap
msgid "classified by a human\n"
"classified by a machine with a degree of certainty of 89%\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:727
#, no-wrap
msgid "taxonID"
msgstr "ID de taxón"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:730
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:taxonID]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:732
msgid "An identifier for <<section-scientificname,scientificName>>. This identifier allows users to find all observations (and media) for a specific taxon. Use a <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>, preferably one assigned by an <<table-taxon-reference-sources,authorative source>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with the `taxonID` of the corresponding taxon in {package-taxonomic}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:734
#, no-wrap
msgid "scientificName"
msgstr "scientificName"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:737
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:scientificName]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:739
msgid "The scientific name of the observed <<individual,individual(s)>>. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-scientificName}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:741
#, no-wrap
msgid "kingdom"
msgstr "reino"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:744
msgid "term:dwc[dwc:kingdom]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:746
msgid "The kingdom in which the taxon with the <<section-scientificname,scientificName>> is classified. It allows services like GBIF's https://www.gbif.org/developer/species[species name matching] to disambiguate between homonyms. Most likely `Animalia` for all records, since camera trap data almost never contain <<classification,classifications>> of plants, fungi or other kingdoms."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: 400.en.adoc:748
#, no-wrap
msgid "Audubon Media Description extension"
msgstr "Extensión de Descripción Multimedia de Audubon"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:751
msgid "As described <<section-why-not-a-sampling-event-dataset,above>>, we recommend to use of an {ac-extension} for expressing camera trap data as a <<darwin-core-archive,Darwin Core Archive>>. See <<table-ac-extension-terms>> for term recommendations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:753
msgid "Note that the {ac-extension} can contain duplicates, an important difference with Camtrap DP's {media} where each file is only listed once. Repeated <<section-ac-occurrenceid,occurrenceID>> are the result of a single <<section-media-or-event-based-classification,event-based>> observation being related to multiple media files (e.g. observation `05230014` in <<table-ac-extension>>). Repeated <<section-ac-identifier,identifiers>> are the result of a media file being the source for multiple observations (e.g. multiple species observed in the same image, such as in media file `e68deaed` in <<table-ac-extension>>). The extension should however contain unique <<section-ac-occurrenceid,occurrenceID>>+<<section-ac-identifier,identifier>> combinations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: 400.en.adoc:755
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended terms to use when expressing camera trap data as an {ac-extension}. <<figure-example-image,Source>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: 400.en.adoc:805
#, no-wrap
msgid "|Term\n"
"|Status\n"
"|Example value\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-occurrenceid,occurrenceID>>\n"
"|Required\n"
"|05230014\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-identifier,identifier>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|6d65f3e4\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-type,type>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|StillImage\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-comments,comments>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|marked as favourite\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-rights,rights>> \n"
"|Strongly recommended\n"
"|[.break-all]#https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode#\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-createdate,CreateDate>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|2020-06-12T06:04:32+02:00\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-capturedevice,captureDevice>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|Reconyx-HF2X\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-resourcecreationtechnique,resourceCreationTechnique>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|motion detection\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-accessuri,accessURI>>\n"
"|Required\n"
"|[.break-all]#https://multimedia.agouti.eu/assets/6d65f3e4-4770-407b-b2bf-878983bf9872/file#\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-format,format>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|image/jpeg\n\n"
"|<<section-ac-serviceexpectation,serviceExpectation>>\n"
"|Share if available\n"
"|online\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:813
msgid "A foreign key to the <<section-occurrenceid,occurrenceID>> in the {occurrence-core}, to indicate the relation between the <<observation>> and the <<media-file,media file(s)>> on which it is based. This term can contain duplicates, as this is a many-to-many relationship (see note in <<section-ac-extension>>). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {observations-observationID}, but the relationship between {observations} and {media} can be established in several ways: either directly via {observations-mediaID} or by selecting media that have the same {media-deploymentID} as the observation and a {media-timestamp} that falls between the {observations-eventStart} and {observations-eventEnd} of the observation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:815
#, no-wrap
msgid "identifier"
msgstr "identificador"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:818
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dcterms_identifier[dcterms:identifier]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:820
msgid "An identifier for the <<media-file,media file>>. Use a <<section-stable-unique-identifiers,stable unique identifier>>. This term can contain duplicates, as this is a many-to-many relationship (see note in <<section-ac-extension>>). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {media-mediaID}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:825
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dc_type[dc:type]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:827
msgid "The nature of the resource. Use `StillImage` for <<image,images>>, `MovingImage` for <<video,videos>>. Do not use https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dcterms_type[**dcterms**:type], because that term expects a URL value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:829
#, no-wrap
msgid "comments"
msgstr "comentarios"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:832
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#ac_comments[ac:comments]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:834
msgid "The comments or notes about the media file. In contrast with <<section-eventremarks,eventRemarks>> and <<section-occurrenceremarks,occurrenceRemarks>>, notes about the media files themselves are seldom recorded in <<data-management-system,data management systems>>. The term could be used to indicate if a media file was marked as favourite or noteworthy. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {media-mediaComments} and relates to {media-favorite}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:836
#, no-wrap
msgid "rights"
msgstr "derechos"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:839
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dcterms_rights[dcterms:rights]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:841
msgid "The licence under which the media file is shared. Note that this applies to file referenced in <<section-ac-accessuri,accessURI>>, not the data in the {ac-extension} (these fall under the dataset license). We recommend using the same license for all media files. To enable wide use, we recommend publishing media files under a https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/[Creative Commons Zero waiver] or https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/[Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license] and to provide it as a URL: `https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode` or `https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode` respectively. Do not use https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dc_rights[**dc**:rights], because that term expects a literal value (the full-text copyright statement). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with the `path` of the licence that has the scope `media` in {package-licenses}, although there it is specified for the dataset as whole, rather than per record."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:843
#, no-wrap
msgid "CreateDate"
msgstr "fechaDeCreación"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:846
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#xmp_CreateDate[xmp:CreateDate]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:848
msgid "The date-time on which the media file was created. This information is typically extracted from the <<EXIF>> metadata by the <<data-management-system,data management system>>. Write timestamps in the ISO 8601 format (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`) and include the timezone (`+02:00`) or convert and indicate as UTC (`Z`). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {media-timestamp}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:850
#, no-wrap
msgid "captureDevice"
msgstr "dispositivoDeCaptura"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:853
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#ac_captureDevice[ac:captureDevice]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:855
msgid "The device(s) used to create the media file. We recommend providing the <<camera>> make and model (e.g. `Reconyx-HF2X`). In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {deployments-cameraModel}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:857
#, no-wrap
msgid "resourceCreationTechnique"
msgstr "técnicaDeCreaciónDeRecurso"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:860
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#ac_resourceCreationTechnique[ac:resourceCreationTechnique]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:862
msgid "The method(s) used to create or alter the media file. We recommend using this term to provide the <<trigger>> method that was used to capture the media file, as controlled values: `activity detection` or `time lapse`. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {media-captureMethod}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:864
#, no-wrap
msgid "accessURI"
msgstr "accesoURI"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:867
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#ac_accessURI[ac:accessURI]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:869
msgid "The URI (Uniform Resource Identifier) that provides access to the media file. Although the term allows to point to relative <<file-path,file paths>> or offline storage, we strongly recommend to provide the http/https URL that serves the media file, if available (see <<section-storage>>). Use a http/https URL that serves the media file directly (not a HTML page embedding it), so it can be displayed on occurrence pages at GBIF.org. Camera trap images are typically small enough that it is not necessary to serve a reduced version of the file. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {media-filePath}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:871
#, no-wrap
msgid "serviceExpectation"
msgstr "expectativaDeServicio"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:874
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#ac_serviceExpectation[ac:serviceExpectation]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:876
msgid "The service expectations users may have of the <<section-ac-accessuri,accessURI>>. We recommend using the controlled values `online` for media files that are publicly accessible over http/https and `authenticate` for media files that are kept private over http/https (see <<section-sensitive-media-files>>). In Camtrap DP, these values related to `TRUE` and `FALSE` respectively in {media-filePublic}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =====
#: 400.en.adoc:878
#, no-wrap
msgid "format"
msgstr "formato"

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:881
msgid "https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dc_format[dc:format]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: 400.en.adoc:883
msgid "The file format of the media file. We recommend providing the media type (MIME type) using the controlled values `image/jpeg`, `video/mp4` or `video/mpeg` of the https://ac.tdwg.org/format/[Audiovisual Core Controlled Vocabulary for Dublin Core]. Do not use https://ac.tdwg.org/termlist/#dcterms_format[**dcterms**:format], because that term expects a URL value. In Camtrap DP, this term corresponds with {media-fileMediatype}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: afterword.en.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Acknowledgements"
msgstr "Reconocimientos"

#. type: Plain text
#: afterword.en.adoc:5
msgid "We thank the following people for making suggestions to this guide and/or providing technical support: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7418-1244[Stephen Formel], https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6492-4016[Donald Hobern], https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6590-599X[Kyle Copas], https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1920-5298[Laura Russell], https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0623-6682[Matt Blissett] and members of the https://camtrap-dp.tdwg.org[Camtrap DP Development Team]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: glossary.en.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "Glosario"

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[activity]]activity"
msgstr "[[activity]]actividad"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:5
msgid "Movement in front of a <<camera>>. Movement can cause a <<trigger>> when certain conditions are met (e.g. within the <<detection-zone,detection zone>> and outside the <<quiet-period,quiet period>>). Camera traps are typically <<deployment,deployed>> to capture wildlife activity, but may also record movements of humans, vehicles or vegetation."
msgstr "Movimiento delante de una <<camera>>. El movimiento puede provocar un <<trigger>> cuando se cumplen ciertas condiciones (p. ej. dentro de la <<detection-zone,detection zone>> y fuera del <<quiet-period,quiet period>>). Las cámaras trampa son típicamente <<deployment,deployed>> para capturar la actividad de la vida silvestre, pero también pueden registrar movimientos de humanos, vehículos o vegetación."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[alignment]]alignment"
msgstr "[[alignment]]alineación"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:7
msgid "Physical placement of a <<camera>>. Consists of <<camera-height,camera height>>, <<camera-depth,camera depth>>, <<camera-tilt,camera tilt>> and <<camera-heading,camera heading>>."
msgstr "Colocación física de una <<camera>>. Consiste en <<camera-height,camera height>>, <<camera-depth,camera depth>>, <<camera-tilt,camera tilt>> y <<camera-heading,camera heading>>."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[AI]]artificial intelligence"
msgstr "[[AI]]inteligencia artificial"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:9
msgid "Ability to perceive, synthesize and infer information as demonstrated by machines, as opposed to humans/animals. In camera trap research, AI is mainly applied as <<machine-learning,machine learning>> to perform <<computer-vision,computer vision>> tasks. See also <<section-artificial-intelligence>>."
msgstr "Capacidad de las máquinas para percibir e inferir información, en lugar de los humanos/animales. En la investigación de cámaras trampa, la IA se aplica principalmente como <<machine-learning,machine learning>> para realizar tareas de <<computer-vision,computer vision>>. Vea también la <<section-artificial-intelligence>>."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bait]]bait"
msgstr "[[bait]]cebo"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:11
msgid "Attractant used to encourage animals to investigate a <<location>> or specific point within the <<detection-zone,detection zone>>. Baits may be auditory, olfactory, visual, or some combination of these in nature. Whether bait was used for a <<deployment>> is useful to know for analyses, as it can alter the natural behaviour of animals. Can be expressed as a categorical description (e.g. `acoustic`, `visual`, `scent`) or a boolean. Also referred to as `lure` cite:[meek-2014]. {deployments-baitUse} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr "Atrayente utilizado para animar a los animales a investigar una <<location>> o un punto específico dentro de la <<detection-zone,detection zone>>. Los cebos pueden ser auditivos, olfativos, visuales, o alguna combinación de estas. Es útil saber que se utilizó un cebo en un <<deployment>> para realizar los análisis, ya que puede alterar el comportamiento natural de los animales. Se puede expresar como una descripción categórica (p. ej., `acústica`, `visual`, `aroma`) o un booleano. También se conoce como señuelo cite:[meek-2014]. {deployments-baitUse} en Camtrap DP."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[blank]]blank"
msgstr "[[blank]]en blanco"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:13
msgid "<<media,Media>> without objects of interest. Blanks are typically the result of false <<trigger,triggers>> such as moving vegetation or fluctuating light. Marked as such when <<classification,classifying>> to facilitate excluding them from queries."
msgstr "<<media,Media>> sin objetos de interés. Los \"en blanco\" a menudo son el resultado de <<trigger,triggers>> falsos como movimientos de la vegetación o luz fluctuante. Marcado como tal cuando se <<classification,classifying>> para facilitar excluirlos de las consultas."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camera]]camera"
msgstr "[[camera]]cámara"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:15
msgid "Device designed to automatically capture <<media>> of (wildlife) <<activity>>, typically <<trigger,triggered>> by a combination of heat and motion. Of a certain make and model and uniquely identifiable by e.g. by serial number. Also referred to as `camera trap`, `game camera`, `trail camera`, `scouting camera` or `device`."
msgstr "Dispositivo diseñado para capturar automáticamente <<media>> de actividad (salvaje), normalmente <<trigger,triggered>> por una combinación de calor y movimiento. De una cierta marca y modelo y singularmente identificable por ejemplo, por número de serie. También se la conoce como `cámara trampa`, `cámara de caza`, `cámara de sendero`, `cámara de exploración` o `dispositivo`."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camera-depth]]camera depth"
msgstr "[[camera-depth]]profundidad de la cámara"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:17
msgid "Depth of the (underwater) camera, a component of camera <<alignment>>. Typically expressed in meters below the local water surface. {deployments-cameraDepth} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr "Profundidad de la cámara (bajo el agua), un componente de la <<alignment>> de la cámara. Normalmente se expresa en metros bajo la superficie de agua local. {deployments-cameraDepth} en Camtrap DP."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camera-height]]camera height"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:19
msgid "Height of the camera above the ground, a component of camera <<alignment>>. Can be expressed in meters above the ground or as a categorical description (`knee height` ~ 0.5m, `chest height` ~ 1.5m, `canopy` ~ 3+m in citenp:[wildlife-insights]). {deployments-cameraHeight} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camera-tilt]]camera tilt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:21
msgid "Up or down orientation of the camera, a component of camera <<alignment>>. Can be expressed in degrees or as a categorical description (`parallel` = 0°, `pointed downward` = -90° in citenp:[wildlife-insights]). {deployments-cameraTilt} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camera-heading]]camera heading"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:23
msgid "Horizontal cardinal orientation of the camera, a component of camera <<alignment>>. Can be expressed in degrees from North or as cardinal directions (N, NW, etc.). {deployments-cameraHeading} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camtrap-dp]]Camtrap DP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:25
msgid "Camera Trap Data Package. A community developed <<data-exchange-format,data exchange format>> for camera trap data, maintained under Biodiversity Information Standards (https://www.tdwg.org[TDWG]). See also <<section-camtrap-dp>>, citenp:[bubnicki-2023] and the https://camtrap-dp.tdwg.org[Camtrap DP website]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[classification]]classification"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:27
msgid "The act of classifying camera trap <<media>>, resulting in <<observation,observations>>. Not to be confused with taxonomic classification. Can be performed in different steps and with different levels of precision, e.g. 1. media does/does not contain object(s) of interest (i.e. <<blank>>), 2. object of interest is human/vehicle/animal or unknown, 3. animal is member of certain taxon (e.g. Sus scrofa, Rodentia), 4. animal is of certain sex/life stage, is known <<individual>> x or shows certain behaviour. Classification is typically labour intensive and therefore often aided by <<computer-vision,computer vision>>, <<citizen-science,volunteers>> and/or classifying <<sequence,sequences>> rather than individual <<media-file,media files>>. Also referred to as `image classification`, `annotation` or `identification`. See also <<section-classification>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[citizen-science]]citizen science"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:29
msgid "Scientific research conducted with participation from the public. Also referred to as `community science`, `crowd science`, `crowdsourcing`, or `volunteer monitoring`. In camera trap research, citizen scientists can participate in camera trap <<deployment>> and <<classification>>. See also <<section-citizen-science>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[cloud-computing]]cloud computing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:31
msgid "Performing computing tasks on a distributed IT infrastructure (“cloud service”). Typically at a cost (“pay as you go”) in return for better performance and less maintenance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[computer-vision]]computer vision"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:33
msgid "Processing, analysing and understanding of <<media>> by machines to aid <<classification>>, from object tracking to species identification. A form of artificial intelligence, typically trained with <<machine-learning,machine learning>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[covariates]]covariates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:35
msgid "Ecological variables that may affect the behaviour and detection of animals (e.g. <<bait,bait use>>, <<feature-type,feature type>>, <<habitat-type,habitat>>, canopy cover). Recording covariates is important for further analysis of the data. See also <<section-covariates>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[data-exchange-format]]data exchange format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:37
msgid "Format used to exchange data between systems (e.g. <<camtrap-dp,Camtrap DP>> and <<darwin-core-archive,Darwin Core Archive>>). Requires data transformation from the source system to the format and from the format to the target system. Well designed data exchange formats facilitate <<FAIR>> data exchange, use open formats and provide clear definitions. Also referred to as `data standard` (when approved through a ratification process)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[data-management-system]]data management system"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:39
msgid "Online or desktop application to manage camera trap data. Typically includes functionality to upload <<media>>, add <<deployment>> information, <<classification,classify>> images, export data, invite <<participant,participants>> and manage a <<project>>. See also <<section-data-management-systems>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[data-repository]]data repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:41
msgid "Online system for the long-term archival of (research) data (e.g. https://zenodo.org[Zenodo], https://datadryad.org/[Dryad] and the GBIF https://www.gbif.org/ipt[IPT]). Different from a <<data-management-system,data management system>> which is designed for the management (and not necessarily long-term archival) of data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[darwin-core-archive]]Darwin Core Archive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:43
msgid "Standardized and widely supported <<data-exchange-format,data exchange format>> for biodiversity data, maintained by Biodiversity Information Standards (https://www.tdwg.org[TDWG]). See also <<section-darwin-core-archive>> and the https://dwc.tdwg.org/text/[Darwin Core text guide]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[deployment]]deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:45
msgid "Spatial and temporal placement of a <<camera>> to sample wildlife images. A camera placed at a location between 1 and 15 January 2020 is a different deployment than the same (or different) camera placed at the same location between 15 and 30 January 2020. Deployments end by removing or replacing the camera, changing their position or swapping their memory card. Also referred to as `sampling point` cite:[wearn-2017], `trap station session` cite:[camelot] or `visit` cite:[newkirk-2016]. {deployments} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-deployments>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[deployment-group]]deployment group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:47
msgid "Logical grouping of <<deployment,deployments>>, based on spatial, temporal or thematic criteria. A deployment can belong to multiple deployment groups. `array` cite:[oconnor-2017], `camera trap array` cite:[meek-2014], `cluster` cite:[risc-2019], `paired deployment` cite:[kolowski-2017], `site` and `strata` cite:[sun-2021] are spatial deployment groups. `sampling campaign` cite:[lamelas-2020], `sampling event` cite:[fegraus-2011] and `session` are temporal deployment groups. `subproject` cite:[emammal-design], `survey` cite:[risc-2019,camerabase] and `tags` are thematic deployment groups. `study areas` cite:[newkirk-2016] can be considered a deployment group or <<project>> in its own right. {deployments-deploymentGroups} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-deployment-groups>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[detection-distance]]detection distance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:49
msgid "Furthest distance in the <<detection-zone,detection zone>> at which the <<camera>> detects <<activity>>. {deployments-detectionDistance} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[detection-zone]]detection zone"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:51
msgid "Area of a <<location>> in which a camera <<sensor>> is able to detect <<activity>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[event]]event"
msgstr "[[evento]]evento"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:53
msgid "Action that occurs at a specific <<location>> for a specific duration. In camera trap research, events typically refer to animal <<activity>> recorded through one or more <<trigger,triggers>> and forming a <<sequence>>, but other definitions might be used when analysing data. Events can be indicated with {observations-eventID}, {observations-eventStart} and {observations-eventEnd} in Camtrap DP. In a <<darwin-core-archive,Darwin Core Archive>>, <<deployment,deployments>> can also be considered events."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[EXIF]]EXIF"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:55
msgid "Exchangeable Image File Format. A format for storing metadata about a <<media-file,media file>> (e.g. creation date and time, format, resolution, shutter speed, exposure level, camera model), typically stored as part of the media file. {media-exifData} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[FAIR]]FAIR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:57
msgid "FAIR (meta)data are (meta)data that meet the principles of findability, accessibility, interoperability and reusability. The FAIR Principles put specific emphasis on enhancing the ability of machines to automatically find and use the data, in addition to supporting its reuse by individuals. See citenp:[wilkinson-2016]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[feature-type]]feature type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:59
msgid "Categorical description of a particular physical feature targeted during the deployment, such as burrow, nest site, or water source. {deployments-featureType} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[file-path]]file path"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:61
msgid "String describing the location of a file in a storage system (e.g. `data/deployments.csv`). When served over http/https, the domain name and file path constitute the file URL (e.g. `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tdwg/camtrap-dp/main/example/deployments.csv`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[GDPR]]GDPR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:63
msgid "General Data Protection Regulation. A https://gdpr-info.eu/[European Union regulation] on information privacy, designed to enhance individuals' control and rights over their personal information. See <<section-personal-data>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[habitat-type]]habitat type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:65
msgid "Categorical description of the environment and vegetation of a <<location>>. Classification systems exist to express habitat cite:[eunis-habitat,iucn-habitat] or vegetation type cite:[us-vegetation]. {deployments-habitat} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[image]]image"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:67
msgid "Static <<media-file,media file>> recorded by a <<camera>>. Has no significant duration or audio."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[independence-interval]]independence interval"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:69
msgid "Minimum duration between consecutive <<trigger,triggers>> to be considered belonging to separate <<sequence,sequences>>. This duration (e.g. 120 seconds) can be defined in a <<data-management-system>> to automatically group <<media>> into sequences. This is different from the <<quiet-period,quiet period>>, which is a camera setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[individual]]individual"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:71
msgid "Distinct organism, typically an animal."
msgstr "Organismo perceptible, normalmente un animal."

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[location]]location"
msgstr "[[ubicación]]ubicación"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:73
msgid "Physical place where a <<deployment,deployed>> <<camera>> is located. A location can be described with a name and/or identifier and coordinates in a certain reference system (e.g. decimal latitude and longitude in WGS84). Also referred to as `camera location` cite:[newkirk-2016], `station` cite:[berkel-2014,camera-trap-manager], `project station` cite:[wildcam-project] or `trap station` cite:[camelot]. Deployment location with a {deployments-locationName}, {deployments-locationID}, {deployments-latitude}, {deployments-longitude}, and {deployments-coordinateUncertainty} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-location>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[machine-learning]]machine learning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:75
msgid "Computational technique that makes use of (training) data (e.g. https://lila.science/) and algorithms to imitate the way that humans learn, gradually improving accuracy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[media]]media"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:77
msgid "<<media-file,Media files>> (plural) captured by a <<camera>>. Also referred to as `photos` cite:[newkirk-2016]. {media} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[media-file]]media file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:79
msgid "A (audio)visual file captured by a <<camera>>. Can be an <<image>> or <<video>>. A media file typically has an identifier, file name, timestamp when it was created and associated metadata (e.g. <<EXIF>>). To access a media file, one needs to know its <<file-path,file path>> and have the required access rights. Media with {media-mediaID}, {media-timestamp}, {media-fileName}, {media-filePath} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-media-files>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[media-type]]media type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:81
msgid "Standardized expression of a file format (e.g. `image/jpeg` for an <<image>>). Formerly known as MIME type. {media-fileMediatype} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[observation]]observation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:83
msgid "Result of a <<classification>>, i.e. a record of what can be seen or heard on <<media-file,media-files>>. Has an <<observation-type,observation type>> to differentiate between animal and other observations. {observations} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-observations>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[observation-type]]observation type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:85
msgid "Categorical description of the type of <<observation>>. Recorded as part of the <<classification>>, allowing to differentiate between <<blank,blanks>>, observations of humans or vehicles and animal observations. {observations-observationType} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[organization]]organization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:87
msgid "Entity comprising one or more people that share a particular purpose, such as a company, institution, association or partnership. Organizations can be directly associated with a <<project>> (e.g. as rights holder, publisher) or indirectly via the affiliation of the project <<participant,participants>>. An organization is a {package-contributors} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[participant]]participant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:89
msgid "Person associated with a <<project>>, performing out one or more <<role,roles>>. Participant information typically includes name and contact information and is subject to <<GDPR>>. <<organization,Organizations>> can also be considered participants. Also referred to as `contributor`, sometimes `user`. A participant is a {package-contributors} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-participants-and-roles>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[role]]role"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:91
msgid "Function carried out by a <<participant>> in a <<project>>, such as project lead, data manager or volunteer <<classification,classifying>> media. Participants can have multiple roles and roles are typically associated with different rights in a <<data-management-system,data management system>> (e.g. the right to invite new participants). Also referred to as `participant type`. {package-contributors-role} in Camtrap DP. See also <<section-participants-and-roles>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[project]]project"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:93
msgid "Scientific investigation by a number of <<participant,participants>>, with a defined objective, methodology, and taxonomical, spatial and temporal scope. The objective of camera trap projects is typically to study and understand wildlife. Also referred to as `study`. {package-project} in Camtrap DP, where a dataset is associated with one and only one project. See also <<section-project-metadata>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[quiet-period]]quiet period"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:95
msgid "Predefined duration after a <<trigger>> when <<activity>> detected by the camera sensor is ignored. {deployments-cameraDelay} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[sampling-design]]sampling design"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:97
msgid "Strategy for deploying cameras to facilitate a certain research purpose. Can be expressed as a categorical description (e.g. `simple random`, `systematic random`, `opportunistic`). {package-project-samplingDesign} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[sensitivity]]sensitivity"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:99
msgid "<<trigger>> sensitivity setting used on a camera sensor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[sensor]]sensor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:101
msgid "Device that detects changes in the environment, such as movement, heat, light, sound, or other stimuli. Modern camera traps typically use an integrated passive infrared (PIR) sensor that is designed to detect <<activity>> based on a combination of heat and motion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[sequence]]sequence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:103
msgid "Series of <<media-file,media files>> taken in rapid succession but separated by a time interval less than the set <<independence-interval,independence interval>> and forming an animated record of an <<event>>. Also referred to as `series` cite:[wildtrax]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[setup]]setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:105
msgid "The act of deploying a <<camera>> in the field. Involves <<alignment>>, defining the camera settings and securing the camera to ensure optimal data captures. {observations-cameraSetupType} in Camtrap DP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[site]]site"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:107
msgid "Geographic area containing multiple <<location,locations>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[species-recognition]]species recognition"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:109
msgid "Automated identification and <<classification>> of different animal species based on visual or auditory data captured by camera traps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[subproject]]subproject"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:111
msgid "Type of <<deployment-group,deployment group>> used to subdivide very large projects into more manageable units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[trigger]]trigger"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:113
msgid "<<sensor,Sensor>> condition that prompts a <<camera>> to activate and capture <<media>>. Also used to indicate the series of consecutive <<media-file,media files>> resulting from that trigger. One or more triggers form a <<sequence>>. Also referred to as `burst`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[UUID]]UUID"
msgstr "[[UUID]]UUID"

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:115
msgid "Universally Unique Identifier (UUID). A type of globally unique identifier that can be generated without a central registration authority. Example: `6d65f3e4-4770-407b-b2bf-878983bf9872`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: glossary.en.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[video]]video"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: glossary.en.adoc:117
msgid "Moving <<media-file,media file>> recorded by a <<camera>>. Has a specific duration and can include audio."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: bibliography.en.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "References"
msgstr "Referencias"

